WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.260
To his friends, he was the Blond Beast.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.740
To his enemies, he was the Hangman, or the
Butcher of Prague.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.599
To the man he devoted his life to, he was
the Man with the Iron Heart.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:14.549
During his life, Reinhard Heydrich was known
by many names, too numerous to list here.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:19.890
But you probably associate him with one name
in particular: Heydrich was the Nazi target

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.910
of Operation Anthropoid.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.919
A talented classical musician who threw it
all away to become a military man, Heydrich

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:28.949
was the Nazi ideal made flesh.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:29.949
He was tall.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:30.949
Blond.

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:31.949
Cultured.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:32.949
A lover of Wagner.

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:33.949
He was also brutal.

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:39.100
It was under Heydrich’s watch that the infamous
Einsatzgruppen were formed, under his direction

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.140
that Nazi enemies were killed, and to his
designs that the Holocaust was perpetrated.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.770
Assassinated by the Czechoslovak resistance
in Prague in 1942, Heydrich is a mystery:

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:55.590
a sensitive, cultured boy who somehow grew
up to be one of history’s worst monsters.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:01.039
Join us today as we journey into Prague’s
heart of darkness.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:13.170
A Young Lad of Promise
If you were shown the conditions Heydrich

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.170
was born into and asked to guess what you
thought he’d grow up to be, “genocidal

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.890
maniac” would probably be far down your
list.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:27.079
Born Reinhard Eugen Tristan Heydrich on March
7, 1904, the world baby Reinhard came into

00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:29.020
was one of middle class luxury.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.610
His father Bruno was an opera aficionado who
ran a music conservatory in the German town

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:38.280
of Halle, near Leipzig, while his mother,
Elisabeth, was a pianist from a wealthy family.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:44.330
For young Heydrich, that meant a life of culture,
money, and – most importantly – music.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.399
Music was the air the family breathed.

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:50.719
Bruno wrote his own operas and sang on stage,
while Elisabeth had little Heydrich trained

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:54.610
to exacting classical standards on the violin
and cello.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:59.630
But there was a cloud hovering over the family’s
charmed life, a cloud that only really counts

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.820
as a cloud if you live surrounded by German
nationalists.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.240
Everyone in Halle thought Bruno was Jewish.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.570
You may be thinking “um, so what?”

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.510
But Bruno didn’t feel that way.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.160
He was certain his supposed Jewish background
was why his opera career never really took

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.160
off.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.630
As time went on, he began to loathe the religion
he blamed for his own failings.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.980
And he made sure young Heydrich loathed it
too.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.890
Still, this unpleasantness aside, their family
life was relatively normal.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.890
Elisabeth was a strict mother, determined
her son should succeed, and soon Heydrich

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.750
was not just an accomplished musician, but
a powerful sportsman too.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.260
This normal family appearance only began to
crack in 1914.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.910
Like many Germans, the Heydrichs were at first
excited by WWI’s outbreak, thinking it’d

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.300
be an easy win for their country.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:53.590
But, as first the weeks dragged on, then the
months, and finally the years, that optimism

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:54.590
began to fade.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:01.110
In the winter of 1916-17, fuel and food shortages
brought on by the war led to starvation and

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.590
misery across the nation.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.650
In Halle, work at Bruno’s conservatory dried
up as the economy faltered.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:11.200
As 1917 rolled on, the German population grew
angry at the war’s management.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.120
They began striking, protesting.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.050
Before long, the cities were in turmoil, as
running street battles erupted between far

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.850
right nationalists and Communists.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.330
Halle wasn’t spared.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.410
As a teen, Heydrich watched left and right
extremists battle for control of his city’s

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.410
streets.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:30.770
Unlike his terrified parents, Heydrich found
the clashes intoxicating.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:35.510
In October, 1918, German dreams of winning
the war finally collapsed with a resounding

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.510
crash.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.820
Germany removed the Kaiser from power and
brought in a civilian government tasked with

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.290
negotiating peace.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.070
In the aftermath, whole segments of the military
went into rebellion.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:49.120
Before the war had even ended on November
11, the country was in revolution.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.770
As a Communist uprising seized control of
Berlin, Heydrich decided he had to make a

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.770
stand.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:58.650
In Halle, the now nearly 16 year old boy joined
a local Freikorps unit.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:04.370
Intended as an anti-Communist militia, the
Freikorps soon bloomed into a far right paramilitary

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.750
force that targeted Jews and revolutionaries
alike.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:11.090
For the teenage Heydrich, the experience was
an eye-opener.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:15.590
For the first time in his life, he was surrounded
by people who felt like he did.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:20.470
People who shared his anti-Semitic beliefs,
his dislike of Communists.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.650
His desire to use violence.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.270
By 11 August, the country was back under control.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.270
The Weimar Republic was founded, and Germany
began to adjust to its new life as a democratic

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.270
nation.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:36.510
But the revolution of 1919 had unleashed the
forces of far right nationalism.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:41.430
And Heydrich wasn’t the only one to heed
their siren call.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:48.180
A Sick Republic
The early days of the Weimar Republic were

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.370
marked by a never-ending series of political
wildfires.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:57.180
On March 13, 1920, an ultranationalist putsch
captured Berlin and held the city for a few

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.000
days before the government regained control.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.260
Three years later, another rightwing putsch,
this time in Munich, killed 20 people.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.430
It’s leader?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.720
One Adolf Hitler.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.720
You might be expecting to hear that Heydrich
was in the thick of all this, cheering on

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.730
the Nazis.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.410
Well, you’d be wrong.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:18.850
After the Freikorps disbanded, Heydrich had
hung around in Halle just long enough to get

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.900
his high school diploma, in 1922.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.660
He’d then high-tailed it out of his hometown
as fast as he could.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.330
But he hadn’t gone running to the Nazi party.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.070
Heydrich had joined the German Navy.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.820
By 1922, Weimar Germany was in the grip of
hyperinflation.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.450
The economy was in ruins.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:40.930
Anyone who wanted a roof over their head and
three square meals a day joined the military.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.720
And Heydrich wanted more than that.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.650
Now a lad of 18, he was ambitious.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.370
He wanted to become an admiral.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:51.520
He still flirted with the far right, maintaining
membership of the anti-Semitic Deutscher Schutz

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.620
und Truzbund.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.990
But while most future high-ranking Nazis were
passionate true believers who were willing

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:01.690
to forego a normal life for their cause, Heydrich
wasn’t like that.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.200
He wanted a respectable career with responsibility.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:10.080
When Hitler published Mein Kampf from his
jail cell in 1925, Heydrich didn’t even

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.080
bother to read it.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:15.710
By 1928, Heydrich’s diligent good work had
paid off enough for him to be promoted to

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.190
first lieutenant and assigned to Navy Intelligence.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:22.460
While he was still taunted for his supposed
Jewish roots, the bullying he used to receive

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.930
for his cultured side was long gone.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.050
Now a grown man, Heydrich’s sensitive qualities
were no longer a burden.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.110
In fact, they made him something of a catch.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:36.090
Throughout the late 1920s and early 1930s,
Heydrich sowed his wild oats like a man hoping

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:39.460
to rival the Quakers in breakfast production.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:43.230
It was during this seductive phase that Heydrich
met Lina von Osten.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.590
Aged just 19, Lina was everything Heydrich
wanted in a woman.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.280
She was charming, intelligent, in awe of him.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.330
And she was a fervent National Socialist.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.320
By 1930, the Nazis were well known in Germany.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.450
But they weren’t yet in charge.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.550
When Heydrich first met Lina, he actually
made fun of her for being a Nazi, calling

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.960
the leadership clowns and deriding Goebbels
as a “cripple”.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.889
Little did the ambitious sailor know he was
only a few short months away from joining

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:11.889
those clowns.

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:14.570
In early 1931, Heydrich proposed to Lina.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:18.419
He then forwarded a copy of the engagement
announcement to another girl he was seeing,

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:20.710
as a way of breaking up with her.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:25.240
But Heydrich’s classy methods soon returned
to bite his Germanic arsch when the girl’s

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.900
father found the announcement and hit the
roof.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.520
He actually complained to the Navy!

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.010
And the Navy responded by actually firing
Heydrich!

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.950
On April 30, 1931, Heydrich was discharged.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:40.310
When he got the news, the future Butcher of
Prague locked himself in his room and cried

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.810
like a baby for days on end.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:47.181
When Heydrich finally emerged from his epic
cry-a-thon, Lina was all like “dude, this

00:07:47.181 --> 00:07:48.181
is perfect.

00:07:48.181 --> 00:07:50.680
You can get a job with the Nazis!”

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.220
At first, Heydrich wasn’t enthusiastic.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:57.060
His main sticking point was that he didn’t
think there were good enough career prospects.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:03.470
But Lina kept pushing him and, eventually,
he joined up, becoming member 544,916.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:09.419
It was the beginning of a rise toward infamy.

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:16.460
Making a Monster
At this point, you might be wondering how

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.930
Heydrich the lothario sailor became Heydrich
the Nazi.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.000
The answer is, surprisingly: his grandmother.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:28.150
By the time Heydrich joined the Nazis, his
mother and grandmother were already enthusiastic

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.150
members.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.750
And they’d carried their wealth and connections
into their new lives.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:36.800
Within a month of Heydrich joining, his grandmother
had arranged a private meeting between Heydrich

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.780
and SS leader Heinrich Himmler.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.200
It’s gotta be said, Himmler wasn’t all
that happy.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.950
The only thing that convinced him to go was
that Heydrich’s grandmother had inflated

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:51.470
her grandkid’s connections to Naval intelligence,
which might be useful to the Nazis.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:55.890
When the two met in Munich, Himmler curtly
gave Heydrich twenty minutes to outline a

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:58.390
counterintelligence operation for the Nazi
Party.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:02.730
Twenty minutes later, the Blackshirts’ leader
collected his jaw off the floor and offered

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.880
Heydrich a job.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:06.880
Heydrich had aced the interview.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.290
Despite only ever holding a low position in
Naval Intelligence, he managed to use all

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.980
his knowledge to outline an effective strategy.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.940
When he hit a blank spot in his knowledge,
he improvised, using the plots of half-remembered

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.190
spy novels.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.450
And it worked.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:25.600
Himmler recruited Heydrich into the SD – the
SS intelligence branch – then and there.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.780
It was the beginning of a partnership that
would eventually leave Europe in ruins.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:34.720
Although Himmler is infamous in his own right,
he and Heydrich could be seen as a double

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.370
act: the Laurel and Hardy of mass murder.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:43.050
During the Night of the Long Knives, in 1934,
Himmler and Heydrich worked together to exterminate

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:46.220
the powerholders in the SA – the Nazi Brownshirts.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:50.960
One of those killed was SA leader Ernst Rohm,
godfather to Heydrich’s own child.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:55.250
In the aftermath, Himmler awarded Heydrich
by promoting him to Chief of the Gestapo.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.980
It was just the first in a sequence of events
we’re gonna call “Himmler promoting Heydrich

00:09:58.980 --> 00:09:59.980
like crazy”.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:05.910
In June, 1936, for example, Himmler merged
the SD, the German criminal police, and the

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.540
Gestapo into a single unit and gave it to
Heydrich.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.240
Three years later, in September, 1939, Himmler
consolidated every single intelligence operation

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.580
across the entire Third Reich under Heydrich.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:23.020
The new Reich Security Main Office (RSHA)
was so powerful even other Nazis were kept

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.410
in the dark about its existence.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.480
Not that Heydrich didn’t earn his new position.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:34.920
For a guy who once called the Nazis clowns,
Heydrich had taken to his new job like a fascist

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.120
duck to water.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:40.360
In November, 1938, he’d directly organized
the looting and burning of Jewish property

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.740
known as Kristallnacht.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:47.310
A year later, in August, 1939, Heydrich had
also masterminded the false flag attack on

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:51.270
Geliwitz that gave the Nazis a pretext for
invading Poland.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:56.890
In fact, many of the most infamous Nazi actions
can be traced back to this one opera lover

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:57.890
from Halle.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:02.940
After the invasion of Poland in September
1939, for example, Heydrich was put in charge

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.630
of the Einsatzgruppen.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:09.070
The Einsatzgruppen were death squads that
followed in the wake of invading German armies,

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.620
mopping up enemies of the Reich.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.740
Their brutality was legendary.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:18.600
In the first three months after the occupation
of Poland, they murdered 50,000.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:22.930
When the Nazis pushed east, in 1941, it was
even worse.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:28.220
Over 33,000 Jews were killed in just two days
in Kiev by Einsatzgruppen.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.580
Not that Heydrich’s crimes only happened
abroad.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:36.520
In 1939, as Germany went to war, Heydrich
had instructed his security service to focus

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.640
on the Reich’s internal enemies.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:43.740
In the dying days of that year, officers fanned
out across German territory, liquidating gypsies,

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.810
Freemasons, homosexuals, Jehovah’s Witnesses,
intellectuals.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.770
Taken together, it was a tsunami of bloodshed.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:54.560
A wave of annihilation unlike anything Europe
had seen in generations.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:58.270
And the worst was yet to come.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:06.580
“The Eternal Subhuman”
On November 12, 1938, Reinhard Heydrich reported

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.589
on the Jewish question to a gathering of Nazis.

00:12:09.589 --> 00:12:13.940
Referring to Europe’s Jews as “the eternal
subhuman”, he declared that imprisoning

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:18.440
them wouldn’t be enough, and that the Reich
would have to get rid of them.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:23.520
Not three months later, Hermann Goering took
Heydrich to one side, and told him to “solve

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:24.520
the Jewish problem”.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:29.490
At this stage, what Goering meant was a policy
of forced emigration and brutal tactics that

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.330
would chase the Jews out of Germany.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:37.120
But, even in early 1939, it was clear the
Blond Beast wouldn’t stop at emigration.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.370
It started after the invasion of Poland.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:44.060
As the Einsatzgruppen were unleashing Hell,
Heydrich and Adolf Eichmann quietly worked

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:47.980
together to have all of Austria’s Jews rounded
up and deported.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:52.750
Later that year, Heydrich directed the opening
of ghettoes in Lodz, Krakow, and Warsaw.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:58.430
He ensured conditions within them were so
bad that hundreds of thousands would die of

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.430
disease.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:03.590
Although extermination was not yet official
Reich policy, Heydrich knew what his superiors

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:04.740
really wanted to do.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:09.290
And, alongside his old buddy Himmler, he set
out to ensure it would happen.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:14.770
In May, 1941, Heydrich issued an order forbidding
Jews to leave the Reich, claiming a “final

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.430
solution” was being prepared.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:21.170
On July 31 that year, Nazi high command gave
Heydrich its blessing to devise a workable

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.339
plan for this “final solution.”

00:13:23.339 --> 00:13:28.529
It was from these black and twisted roots
that the poison fruit of the Holocaust was

00:13:28.529 --> 00:13:29.529
born.

00:13:29.529 --> 00:13:34.490
Now, many people were implicit in the Holocaust
– not least Heydrich’s BFF Himmler – and

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:38.350
we wouldn’t want to let them off the hook
by making it appear like it was Heydrich’s

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.910
work alone.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:44.620
That being said, the Blond Beast was intimately
involved in planning the 20th Century’s

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:45.970
worst genocide.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:51.180
On January 20, 1942, Heydrich summoned leading
Nazis to the Berlin suburb of Wannsee for

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.230
a conference.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:56.709
Over a three course lunch, Heydrich led a
genial discussion on his plans to rid Europe

00:13:56.709 --> 00:13:57.830
of its Jews.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.720
His idea was to march all 11 million east,
letting them die through starvation and exposure

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:03.720
along the way.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:08.420
The survivors would then be interred in labor
camps and worked to death, with any that persistently

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:11.790
survived finally exterminated by hand.

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:16.259
When the Wannsee Conference disbanded, the
fate of the Reich’s Jews had been sealed.

00:14:16.259 --> 00:14:21.080
The Holocaust was now official Nazi policy,
and it’s chief architect was determined

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.290
to get started as soon as possible.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:28.120
But Heydrich wasn’t going to live to see
his murderous idea made flesh.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:32.610
Vengeance was about to come from a very unlikely
source.

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:39.480
The “Vermin”
Reinhard Heydrich wasn’t aware of it as

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:44.279
he stepped out into the cold Berlin air after
the Wannsee Conference, but, far away, two

00:14:44.279 --> 00:14:46.600
men were already plotting his murder.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.420
Their names were Jan Kubiš, and Jozef Gabčík.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:53.520
They were former Czechoslovak citizens who’d
escaped abroad and been trained by British

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:54.520
Intelligence.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:57.029
And they were going to kill the Blond Beast.

00:14:57.029 --> 00:15:01.310
The wheels of fate that would set Heydrich,
Kubiš, and Gabčík on a collision course

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.311
had first begun turning nearly three and a
half years earlier.

00:15:04.311 --> 00:15:09.670
In early October, 1938, the governments of
France and Britain had agreed to the German

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.900
annexation of Czechoslovakia’s Sudetenland
region.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:16.751
Of course, this soon turned out to be a case
of “give a Nazi an inch, and they’ll take

00:15:16.751 --> 00:15:21.490
your entire country,” and five months later,
German troops invaded Czechoslovakia.

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:26.290
In Slovakia, a Nazi puppet regime was installed,
while the area of modern-day Czech Republic

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:31.290
became the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia,
under direct German rule.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:35.279
The German invasion of Czechoslovakia wasn’t
as brutal as later invasions, like those of

00:15:35.279 --> 00:15:37.200
Poland and the USSR.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.860
Czech industry was considered too vital to
the German war effort to risk disrupting,

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:46.019
so the Nazi mass executions of the period
usually involved dozens, rather than hundreds

00:15:46.019 --> 00:15:47.410
or thousands of victims.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:52.490
In fact, the Nazis were so comparatively soft
touch in the Protectorate that a healthy resistance

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.850
movement sprang up, engaging in frequent acts
of sabotage.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.100
It was this sabotage that brought Heydrich
onto the scene.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:04.800
On September 24, 1941, Hitler sacked the former
Protector of Bohemia and Moravia in a fit

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:09.240
of pique at all these insolent Czechs playing
Švejk to his glorious Reich.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:14.079
In place of the old guy, Heydrich was called
in to whip Prague into shape.

00:16:14.079 --> 00:16:15.279
Heydrich was not a fan of Czechs.

00:16:15.279 --> 00:16:19.550
Prior to his posting, he’d referred to his
new subjects as “the Czech vermin”.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:24.490
On arriving in Prague, he arranged to have
142 people hanged in just five days.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:25.920
It was a mission statement.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:30.890
A promise of the blood that would flow through
the cobbled streets of Prague if the Czechs

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.910
didn’t start playing nice.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.230
It was also Heydrich’s own death warrant.

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:38.839
In London, the Czechoslovak government in
exile watched Heydrich take his new posting

00:16:38.839 --> 00:16:40.820
with a feeling of impotence.

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:45.050
Already, the exiled Czechs and Slovaks were
unpopular among their British hosts for their

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:47.460
apparent unwillingness to take hard action.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:51.510
While Polish pilots were shooting down German
bombers and the French Resistance was engaging

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:56.300
in life or death escapades, the Czechs were
seemingly content to just sabotage a few factories.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:17:00.870
The exiled government needed a piece of concrete
heroism they could show the world, to prove

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:04.589
they weren’t the weak partners in the fight
against Nazi rule.

00:17:04.589 --> 00:17:07.239
In Heydrich, they found the perfect cause.

00:17:07.239 --> 00:17:11.909
On October 3, 1941, the exiled Czechoslovak
government informed Britain’s Special Operations

00:17:11.909 --> 00:17:14.209
Executive that they were going to assassinate
Heydrich.

00:17:14.209 --> 00:17:17.859
The Brits were all like “you guys are actually
gonna do something?

00:17:17.859 --> 00:17:19.059
Great, let’s kill a Nazi!”

00:17:19.059 --> 00:17:23.319
Less than a month later, Slovak warrant officer
Jozef Gabčík was chosen for the special

00:17:23.319 --> 00:17:24.319
mission.

00:17:24.319 --> 00:17:28.539
He was initially joined by Czech soldier Karel
Svoboda, but Svoboda injured himself and was

00:17:28.539 --> 00:17:31.210
replaced by Czech Staff Sargant Jan Kubiš.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:35.739
Two months later, just after Christmas, Kubiš
and Gabčík parachuted alongside several

00:17:35.739 --> 00:17:41.020
Czechoslovak commandos into the wintery landscape
outside Prague under the cover of night.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:45.259
As the men moved silently through the snow
towards the distant glow of the ancient city,

00:17:45.259 --> 00:17:48.600
the citizens of Bohemia slept soundly in their
beds.

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.999
No-one could have known what a firestorm was
about to be unleashed.

00:17:52.999 --> 00:17:59.580
“Resembling a human”
The name chosen for the plan to assassinate

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:03.850
Heydrich was Operation Anthropoid, a word
which means “resembling a human.”

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:08.730
It was the perfect name for a plan to assassinate
the most inhuman human of all.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:13.220
Back in Prague, Heydrich had spent his few
short months as Protector pacifying first

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.240
the city, then the country.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:20.720
The capital had seen the promised bloodshed,
with some 400 civilians sent to the gallows.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:24.059
In the wider Protectorate, around 5,000 had
been imprisoned and tortured.

00:18:24.059 --> 00:18:27.309
But Heydrich hadn’t just gone in guns blazing
and noose swinging.

00:18:27.309 --> 00:18:31.669
It was widely accepted that treating the Czechs
like the Poles would hamper the German war

00:18:31.669 --> 00:18:32.669
effort.

00:18:32.669 --> 00:18:34.409
So he’d deployed kindness, too.

00:18:34.409 --> 00:18:36.559
Under Heydrich, rations had been increased.

00:18:36.559 --> 00:18:37.980
Wages raised.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:38.980
Pensions subsidized.

00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:43.580
It was a cynical move straight out the far
right playbook: stuff gold down the population’s

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.909
throats to distract them from your crimes.

00:18:45.909 --> 00:18:47.509
It had also worked.

00:18:47.509 --> 00:18:51.980
As spring, 1942 rolled into view, Heydrich
was able to report the Czechs were pacified.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:56.110
His carrot and machinegun tactics had seen
sabotage rates plummet.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.700
Factory productivity was booming.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:03.210
Nazi occupation seemed so accepted that Heydrich
even felt comfortable motoring around Prague

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:07.779
in an open topped car, with only a handgun
and his armed driver for protection.

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:11.679
But Prague wasn’t quite as pacified as Heydrich
thought.

00:19:11.679 --> 00:19:15.929
Somewhere in the old alleyways of the city,
Kubiš and Gabčík laid low in the house

00:19:15.929 --> 00:19:18.950
of an unsuspecting family, plotting their
next move.

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:23.789
They’d made contact with the Czech Resistance
months ago, and were now feeling deeply frustrated.

00:19:23.789 --> 00:19:27.960
A plan to assassinate Heydrich on a road near
his house had been called off at the last

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:28.960
minute.

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:30.980
Another plan to kill him on a train had been
aborted.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:35.370
They’d now been in Prague nearly five months,
and Heydrich was still alive.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:40.169
It was at this point that someone suggested
killing Heydrich on his morning drive to work.

00:19:40.169 --> 00:19:42.739
On Heydrich’s regular route, there was a
hairpin corner.

00:19:42.739 --> 00:19:44.991
Anyone driving around it would have to slow
to a near-crawl.

00:19:44.991 --> 00:19:50.179
In other words, it was the perfect place to
kill someone in an open top car.

00:19:50.179 --> 00:19:55.850
On the morning of May 27, 1942, Gabčík and
Kubiš waited in a tram stop by the corner.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:59.460
They were dressed in civilian clothes, but
there was nothing innocent about them.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:04.149
Under his coat, Gabčík had a Sten gun, while
Kubiš had an anti-tank grenade hidden in

00:20:04.149 --> 00:20:05.149
a briefcase.

00:20:05.149 --> 00:20:09.519
As the city came to life around them, the
two men waited for their date with destiny.

00:20:09.519 --> 00:20:11.850
Shortly after they arrived, Heydrich’s car
came into view.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.779
As predicted, the driver slowed for the corner.

00:20:14.779 --> 00:20:18.659
Gabčík casually stepped into the street,
turned, and opened fire with his submachinegun.

00:20:18.659 --> 00:20:20.440
At least, that was the plan.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.989
What really happened was Gabčík’s gun
jammed.

00:20:23.989 --> 00:20:27.729
As he frantically tried to fire the fatal
shot, Heydrich’s expression turned from

00:20:27.729 --> 00:20:30.139
one of surprise to white hot anger.

00:20:30.139 --> 00:20:33.960
Ordering his driver to stop, Heydrich grabbed
his own gun, and raised it at Gabčík.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:38.690
The Slovak just had time to see the barrel
train on him when the explosion hit.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.029
The second Heydrich’s car had stopped, Kubiš
had hurled his briefcase bomb.

00:20:42.029 --> 00:20:43.850
He was actually off target.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:48.669
The grenade exploded behind the car, knocking
all three men down, but killing no-one.

00:20:48.669 --> 00:20:52.590
Heydrich staggered to his feet and opened
fire on Kubiš, but blast had stunned him

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:54.259
and the bullets went wild.

00:20:54.259 --> 00:20:57.639
Kubiš grabbed a bicycle and escaped, certain
the assassination had failed.

00:20:57.639 --> 00:21:01.720
Screaming at his driver to get that bastard!,
Heydrich ran after Gabčík, firing at the

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.029
Slovak’s sprinting form.

00:21:03.029 --> 00:21:06.710
They ran one street, two… when something
odd happened.

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:09.740
Heydrich, the consummate sportsman, found
he couldn’t run.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.669
He was out of breath.

00:21:11.669 --> 00:21:15.000
After a couple of hundred meters, he collapsed
on the ground, raised a hand to his side.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.179
It came away sticky with blood.

00:21:17.179 --> 00:21:20.869
The briefcase bomb had missed its target,
but the shrapnel hadn’t.

00:21:20.869 --> 00:21:25.629
As the rear of the car was torn to bits, a
lump of jagged metal had been propelled deep

00:21:25.629 --> 00:21:27.309
inside Heydrich’s body.

00:21:27.309 --> 00:21:33.179
The Blond Beast didn’t know it, but he was
already dead.

00:21:33.179 --> 00:21:38.649
Massacre
In the end, it took Reinhard Heydrich eight

00:21:38.649 --> 00:21:40.759
whole days to die.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:42.970
For a while, it actually looked as if he might
recover.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:49.200
But then septicemia set in and the cultured
young man from Halle passed away on June 4.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.359
The response was immediate.

00:21:51.359 --> 00:21:54.679
In Berlin, Hitler demanded the heads of 10,000
Czechs.

00:21:54.679 --> 00:21:59.200
On June 10, SS units walked into the Czech
village of Lidice and fulfilled the Fuhrer’s

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.200
demand.

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:04.710
All the men and boys of Lidice were shot dead,
all the women and girls loaded into trucks

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.580
and sent to concentration camps.

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:10.369
When it was discovered 11 men were outside
the village on business, Nazi agents were

00:22:10.369 --> 00:22:13.309
sent to track them down and murder them too.

00:22:13.309 --> 00:22:16.590
All the pets and animals in the village were
rounded up and shot.

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:18.519
Finally the buildings were set on fire.

00:22:18.519 --> 00:22:23.399
The Nazis filmed the whole thing, intending
Lidice to be a warning to the world.

00:22:23.399 --> 00:22:27.830
In Prague, revenge mass killings were carried
out, resulting in 1,300 dead.

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:31.389
Another Czech village – Ležáky – was
targeted and also destroyed.

00:22:31.389 --> 00:22:35.649
It was like the Angel of Death had swept across
the land, like Heydrich’s poisonous soul

00:22:35.649 --> 00:22:39.860
was carrying out one last killing spree before
returning to Hell.

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:43.629
Three weeks after the assassination, a Czech
collaborator, Karel Čurda, passed on the

00:22:43.629 --> 00:22:46.450
hiding place of Gabčík and Kubiš to the
Gestapo.

00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:50.320
The two assassins were in the basement of
Prague’s Cathedral Church of Sts Cyril and

00:22:50.320 --> 00:22:51.320
Methodius.

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:55.289
On June 18, 1942, 700 soldiers converged on
the church.

00:22:55.289 --> 00:22:59.419
Gabčík and Kubiš held them off for some
hours before committing suicide in the Cathedral

00:22:59.419 --> 00:23:00.419
crypt.

00:23:00.419 --> 00:23:04.009
The bullet holes from the firefight can still
be seen today.

00:23:04.009 --> 00:23:07.989
In the West, the reaction to Heydrich’s
assassination was equally swift and decisive.

00:23:07.989 --> 00:23:12.539
The image of Lidice in flames spurred the
Allies to tear up the Munich Agreement.

00:23:12.539 --> 00:23:17.340
Until this moment in 1942, it was still possible
that a postwar settlement might allow the

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:19.500
Germans to keep the Sudetenland.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.990
With images of Lidice fresh in everyone’s
minds, that was no longer an option.

00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:29.590
It was thanks to this one assassination that
Czechoslovakia was able to remain a nation

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:30.669
after WWII.

00:23:30.669 --> 00:23:32.020
But what about Heydrich?

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:36.889
Heydrich was the only high ranking Nazi to
be assassinated in the whole of WWII, a fact

00:23:36.889 --> 00:23:39.850
that explains our continued fascination with
him.

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:43.779
But beyond Operation Anthropoid, Heydrich
deserves to be remembered.

00:23:43.779 --> 00:23:47.070
He was the man who outlined the blueprint
for the Holocaust.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:50.690
The man who controlled the infamous Einsatzgruppen.

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:54.429
It was under his watch that the notorious
Polish ghettoes were created.

00:23:54.429 --> 00:23:59.960
Had he lived longer, it’s undoubtable that
he would have committed more atrocities.

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.889
Unlike nearly every other leading Nazi, there’s
no indication Heydrich was a true believer

00:24:03.889 --> 00:24:04.889
in the early days.

00:24:04.889 --> 00:24:10.529
More an opportunist who took a job to please
his fiancée and then did that job with bloodthirsty

00:24:10.529 --> 00:24:11.529
relish.

00:24:11.529 --> 00:24:15.269
In many ways, that makes him even scarier
than someone like his old buddy Himmler.

00:24:15.269 --> 00:24:21.229
We like to think of people as either inherently
good or inherently evil, but Heydrich wasn’t

00:24:21.229 --> 00:24:22.450
inherently anything.

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:23.879
He was just a blank, a hollow man.

00:24:23.879 --> 00:24:28.980
In another life he probably would have made
a boringly average Naval commander.

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:31.070
But Heydrich didn’t live another life.

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:33.840
He lived this one, with all its bloodshed.

00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:38.869
In the end, perhaps all we can say is that
the shy, sensitive boy from Halle was simply

00:24:38.869 --> 00:24:40.259
the perfect anthropoid.

00:24:40.259 --> 00:24:52.859
A creature that looked human without ever
feeling even the faintest flicker of humanity.

